f(2,'workedExample','A classic full checker must inspect broadly enough to reconcile inode/block ownership, directories and allocation metadata. Its cost depends on metadata volume, layout, algorithms and hardware, not just the damaged bytes. Journal replay usually bounds normal crash-recovery work to relevant log transactions, but neither a fixed runtime nor freedom from all later full checks follows. The stated three-hour result is hypothetical.','No seconds howeverbig/strictlinear.',th)
