f(11,'explanation','CoW updates can fragment layout. NOCOW must be configured on empty/new files or inherited by newly created files; it disables data checksums and compression for that data. Snapshot-shared extents still require COW when modified. Measure layout and I/O before changing policy.','Snapshotstillcow/directorynotretroactive.',bt,o=1)
f(11,'workedExample','Random CoW updates can replace adjacent logical blocks with scattered extents, but measure fragmentation and storage behavior before attributing slowdown. A directory NOCOW attribute affects newly created files; it does not convert existing populated files. NOCOW disables data checksums/compression and still needs COW for shared extents. Defragmentation may unshare extents and increase space use. Filesystem migration and database-record-size tuning require workload-specific validation; database WAL does not replace all filesystem integrity features. No measured seek latency or universal tuning value is supplied.','Remove10ms/mythallNOCOW/same ZFSsize universal.',bt+zf)
f(12,'prompt',json.loads(Path(q).read_text())[11]['prompt']+' Assume the naive protocol has neither an ordering guarantee nor transaction-integrity verification.','Else checksummedfine.',th)
f(12,'explanation','Correct. A commit marker alone is insufficient if it can persist before its dependencies. An asynchronous checksummed journal can reject incomplete transactions, but it still needs a complete durable commit before acknowledging success. journal_async_commit and journal_checksum are distinct settings.','Correctasyncnotjustchecksum.',ext,o=1)
f(12,'workedExample','In the naive protocol, the commit marker can persist while some logged blocks do not, allowing invalid replay. One remedy orders and flushes log contents before the durable commit record. An asynchronous protocol can use transaction checksums to reject incomplete records, but must still ensure all required writes are stable before promising durability. Checksums detect incomplete/corrupt records; they do not themselves persist data or universally make commits faster.','Checksumnotdurability/guaranteedspeed.',ext)
